      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Also, a bit of correction, it's still possible to just upload a Good performance ranked Quest avatar and a Very Poor PC avatar together and use it as a fallback and the avatar parameters would sync just fine, but still, in this way a lot of functionalities would break between these two, like phys bones would stop moving if I would exceed the limits.\n\nSo, in the end, it would be still better if I could separately upload a full version of the avatar with usually 500+ phys bone transforms and also have a lower quality fallback of this avatar that doesn't exceed the 256 phys bone transform limit, so the phys bones would be still able to move on the fallback\n\nbut yeah, another extra thing is to make like the phys bones sync together too with these fallbacks",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-09-06T00:31:03.931Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If people have completely identical avatars, let's say PC full version (Very Poor performance ranked) of the avatar and an optimized version for the same avatar, then we should have the option to link the full version of the avatar to that specific fallback, so the parameters would sync together, so the face track and other parameters would still work on these fallbacks.\n\nCurrently, even if the parameters 100% matches between the full version and fallback avatar, the sync just still won't happen\n\nIt would be a good thing, since random people with weaker hardware could also see the parameter changes on the fallbacks, and your friends could just enable your avatar to see it's full functionality, keeping the balance between performance and quality this way.",
